{
  "format": "data_gen_release_sources_v1",
  "project_root": "<project> (the LeWM manipulation research repository; paths are relative to it)",
  "notes": [
    "Every code file (*.py) is a byte-identical copy of the project file (sha256_src == sha256_dst) except the entries whose 'edit' field starts with 'release:': four edited copies (convert_rrt_branches.py, tests/test_convert_rrt_branches.py, wm_training/tests/test_danger_strata.py and the new wm_training/label_audit.py; every changed or added line of those files carries a '# release:' comment) and two files written for this release with no project source (make_video.py, tests/test_make_video.py; 'src' = '(new in this release)', sha256_src / bytes_src = null).",
    "make_video.py (new, root) renders the generated data on a machine without a display: GIFs and contact-sheet PNGs with a label bar (state index / time, worst pillar tilt, UNSAFE, grasped, branch or family name) for a raw episode directory, a dataset directory (counterfactual branches side by side with --grid), an anchor_XXXX.npz (all rollouts as a grid) and a training-cache episode .h5; numpy + Pillow + h5py only. quickstart.sh step 21 runs it into smoke_out/videos; tests/test_make_video.py (new) exercises it on synthetic frames without the simulator and is in the --with-tests list.",
    "Documentation is the English README.md only; the project's Chinese specifications are not shipped.",
    "Not shipped (this release is the data-generation code only): the model-training and evaluation modules of wm_training (finetune_tilt, finetune_dataset, tilt_head, train, decoder, numerics, evaluate_bench_wm, evaluate_short, short_report, score_bench, eval_cache, check_encoder_digest, safety_classifier, evaluate_danger_strata) and the two tests that need them (wm_training/tests/test_bench_cache.py, test_counterfactual_cache.py). convert_rrt_branches.py's post-conversion audit, which imported eval_cache / finetune_dataset / finetune_tilt, is skipped and recorded (see its entry).",
    "Not shipped: rrt_data_plan.py (the campaign quota planner; the frozen plan it produced is not shipped either) and compare_rrt_branches.py (the re-collection comparison tool), with tests/test_rrt_data_plan.py and tests/test_compare_rrt_branches.py.",
    "collect_random_branches.py / random_branches_plan.py are shipped as library code imported by rrt_branches_plan.py and collect_rrt_branches.py; their own random-action branch datasets were evaluation pools, not S1 training data.",
    "goal_carry.py (listed as shared in the brief) is not imported by anything in this closure (only by the planner / goal-image / video tools, out of scope) and is therefore not shipped.",
    "wm_training/tests/test_provenance.py is not shipped: it imports wm_training.evaluate_stop_policy (out of scope)."
  ],
